98 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 19 0 R/T(Long before British arrival, Fort Canning Hill was known as Bukit Larangan, or \217Forbidden Hill\220. Historical traditions and archaelogoical finds suggest that the hill was an important royal centre in 14th - century Singapura. Sang Nila Utama Garden re-imagines a Southeast Asian palace garden, while Pancur Larangan evokes the spring linked to royal bathing traditions. The nearby keramat is traditionally associated with Iskandar Shah, remembered as one of the last Malay rulers connected to Singapore.)/E(Long before British arrival, Fort Canning Hill was known as Bukit Larangan, or \217Forbidden Hill\220. Historical traditions and archaelogoical finds suggest that the hill was an important royal centre in 14th - century Singapura. Sang Nila Utama Garden re-imagines a Southeast Asian palace garden, while Pancur Larangan evokes the spring linked to royal bathing traditions. The nearby keramat is traditionally associated with Iskandar Shah, remembered as one of the last Malay rulers connected to Singapore.)/Pg 7 0 R/K[17 19 18]>>
endobj

