596 0 obj
<</Title(After the military fort lost its strategic value, much of the old citadel was dismantled in the 1920s. The hilltop was then adapted for civic infrastructure with the construction of the Fort Canning Service Reservoir. The change marks a new phase in which the hill shifted from defence to public utility.)/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 552 0 R>>
endobj

597 0 obj
<</Title(Completed in the late 1920s, the reservoir increased Singapore\220s water-storage capacity. Its construction altered the military landscape and explains why only parts of the former fort survive today.)/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 553 0 R/Next 598 0 R>>
endobj

598 0 obj
<</Title(The open green above it now hides an important layer of the hill\220s modern history.)/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 553 0 R/Prev 597 0 R/First 615 0 R/Last 615 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

